-{"species":"garchomp","moves":["dragonclaw","earthquake","protect","rockslide"],"item":"sitrusberry","regulation":"champions-reg-ma","spread":{"hp":19,"atk":26,"def":0,"spa":0,"spd":0,"spe":21},"source_tier":"champions_native_writeup","verified":false,"verification_context":{},"date_resolved":"2026-07-27T18:28:16Z","rationale":"Bulky Garchomp utilizes its high Speed and Attack in conjunction with defensive items to become an all-rounder that can be brought to almost any matchup, with coverage to threaten top Pokemon like Sneasler, Mega Charizard Y, opposing Garchomp, and sometimes even Mega Floette. Rock Slide vs Stomping Tantrum: Rock Slide allows Garchomp to fish for flinches and threaten Mega Charizard Y with serious damage. Stomping Tantrum, on the other hand, offers a secondary, single-target Ground-type STAB option, bypassing Wide Guard from Aegislash and Aerodactyl and giving Garchomp the ability to threaten Ground-type damage without also threatening its partner with Earthquake. Protect vs Poison Jab: Protect is an amazing tool for any team, allowing Garchomp to defensively position itself throughout the game. Poison Jab can be run to threaten Fairy-types, namely Mega Floette, Sylveon, and Whimsicott; it is only run on Garchomp sets with Roseli Berry, because Poison Jab commonly misses OHKOs and Roseli Berry lets Garchomp take a Fairy-type attack before finishing the job with another Poison Jab. Other Options Rock Tomb: Rock Tomb, similar to Rock Slide, provides coverage against Mega Charizard Y but avoids Wide Guard from the likes of Aerodactyl. It also provides a form of Speed control but is really only useful against Mega Charizard Y because of its inability to fish for flinches or damage both foes. Items Sitrus Berry: Sitrus Berry grants Garchomp far more longevity by allowing it to avoid 2HKOs from attacks such as Close Combat from Sneasler. Roseli Berry: Roseli Berry allows Garchomp to take on the format's Fairy-types when used in combination with Poison Jab in one-on-one scenarios. Abilities Rough Skin: Rough Skin punishes attacks like Close Combat and Liquidation from Sneasler and Basculegion-M, respectively, breaking their Focus Sashes. It also punishes Fake Out from Incineroar; at low HP, Incineroar often cannot afford to use Fake Out on Garchomp without KOing itself. SP Spreads 19 HP / 26 Atk / 21 Spe with Jolly: The Attack investment allows Garchomp to OHKO uninvested Mega Charizard Y with Rock Slide, while the Speed investment lets it outrun maximum Speed Hisuian Arcanine. The bulk allows Garchomp to almost always survive Last Respects from Basculegion-M after two of its allies have fainted and always survive Knock Off from Jolly Mega Tyranitar after a Dragon Dance. Teambuilding Checks and Weaknesses: Even with Roseli Berry, Garchomp can struggle against Fairy-types, as Poison Jab doesn't OHKO them, leaving Garchomp vulnerable to being OHKOed by Mega Floette's Light of Ruin and Sylveon's Hyper Beam. Garchomp also struggles to damage Mega Froslass, which can OHKO it with Blizzard. Opposing Dragon-types like Mega Dragonite, Archaludon, and Hydreigon can be issues for Garchomp, as they can survive Dragon Claw or Earthquake and retaliate with Draco Meteor. Without an offensive item like Soft Sand, Garchomp may also struggle to deal damage to the likes of Incineroar and Mega Scovillain, especially after being affected by Intimidate or a burn, respectively. Good Partners and Synergies: Mega Charizard Y is a great partner for Garchomp, resisting the Fairy-type attacks that threaten Garchomp, OHKOing Mega Froslass and Alolan Ninetales, and, when the two are next to each other, allowing Garchomp to use Earthquake freely. Fairy-type partners like Whimsicott and Mega Floette can threaten opposing Dragon-types, while partners like Mega and base Glimmora and as well as Sneasler can threaten opposing Fairy-types. How to Overcome Garchomp's Weaknesses: Keeping Garchomp in the back and removing threats to it early on are good ideas, as its amazing coverage lets it easily clean up a lot of the format's common Pokemon. Having switch-ins to Fairy-types is also a must, as they pose a huge threat to Garchomp even with Roseli Berry. Garchomp also appreciates allies that can stay on the field alongside it while it continuously deals damage with Earthquake, such as Mega Aerodactyl, which can provide Tailwind, use Rock Slide to hit opposing Flying-types, and use Dual Wingbeat to weaken and threaten Sinistcha, a Pokemon Garchomp can struggle to hit.","source_format":"champions/vgc-2026-regulation-m-a"}
