 {"species":"kingambit","moves":["ironhead","kowtowcleave","protect","suckerpunch"],"item":"chopleberry","regulation":"champions-reg-ma","spread":{"hp":32,"atk":32,"def":2,"spa":0,"spd":0,"spe":0},"source_tier":"champions_native_writeup","verified":false,"verification_context":{},"date_resolved":"2026-07-27T18:28:17Z","rationale":"Kingambit is one of the top threats of Regulation M-A, trading damage comfortably and threatening many top threats such as Basculegion-M, Aegislash, and Mega Floette. Additionally, Kingambit's typing allows it to defensively answer both Glimmora's and Mega Gengar's STAB moves. Sucker Punch: Sucker Punch makes up for Kingambit's poor Speed and threatens faster Pokemon such as Basculegion-M. Sucker Punch is also useful for late-game one-on-ones, as it pressures the opponent to guess whether Kingambit will choose Kowtow Cleave or Sucker Punch. Iron Head versus Low Kick: Iron Head is used to threaten Mega Floette, Mega Meganium, and Sylveon while dealing decent damage to Sneasler. Low Kick is used to threaten opposing Kingambit, Incineroar, and Tyranitar. However, Kingambit cannot damage the Fairy-types and Sneasler much if it opts for Low Kick. Other Options Swords Dance: Swords Dance allows Kingambit to become a setup sweeper. This move is typically seen with Black Glasses to maximize damage, as Black Glasses- and Swords Dance-boosted Sucker Punch can OHKO Mega Charizard Y and frailer Garchomp. However, Low Kick and Iron Head tend to be more consistent moves and preferred over Swords Dance, as Kingambit prefers trading damage rather than becoming a setup sweeper in this metagame. SP Spreads 20 HP / 25 Atk / 21 Spe with Adamant: This alternative SP spread allows Kingambit to outspeed bulkier Mega Gengar in Tailwind and some Corviknight, and the HP investment lets it survive bulky Sneasler's Close Combat with Chople Berry. The rest of the SPs have been put into Attack to maximize damage. Items Chople Berry: In conjunction with its standard SP spread, Kingambit can survive Jolly Sneasler's Close Combat, as well as opposing Kingambit's and Tyranitar's Low Kick. Black Glasses: Black Glasses allows Kingambit to deal more damage with Kowtow Cleave and Sucker Punch. Black Glasses-boosted Sucker Punch always OHKOes Choice Scarf Basculegion-M and can OHKO snow-boosted Mega Froslass most of the time. Abilities Defiant: This ability allows Kingambit to punish Icy Wind Milotic, Incineroar, and even Moonblast's Special Attack drops from Mega Floette and Whimsicott. Defiant's boost allows Kingambit to OHKO Sinistcha with Kowtow Cleave. Teambuilding Checks and Weaknesses: Even with Chople Berry, Kingambit does not have the best matchup against Sneasler. Low Kick from opposing Kingambit and Tyranitar and Close Combat from Aegislash threaten to OHKO Kingambit as well. Without Iron Head, Mega Floette and Sylveon will outdamage Kingambit. Mega Charizard Y is faster than Kingambit and will threaten to OHKO it, while Excadrill and Garchomp are Ground-types that threaten it super effectively. Even though Kingambit has a decent matchup against Tyranitar, losing speed control can result in Kingambit losing, since Tyranitar can hit it with Low Kick before it can move. Good Partners and Synergies: Kingambit likes being on balance-oriented teams where it can utilize its great bulk. Basculegion-M can cover for Kingambit's Fighting, Fire, and Ground weaknesses; Mega Charizard Y can cover for its Fighting and Ground weaknesses; and Mega Floette and Sylveon can cover for its Fighting weakness. Basculegion-M and Sinistcha can block Sneasler's Close Combat and, in Sinistcha's case, set up Trick Room for Kingambit. Garchomp can threaten opposing Kingambit, Mega Charizard Y, Sneasler, and Tyranitar. Basculegion-M and Sneasler are Kingambit's best partners overall, as Sneasler can threaten opposing Kingambit and Mega Scovillain, while Basculegion-M can threaten Excadrill and Glimmora. How to Overcome Kingambit's Weaknesses: Position Kingambit out of the face of Sneasler to let Kingambit's partners take care of it. Aerodactyl can OHKO Sneasler with Dual Wingbeat and set up Tailwind for Kingambit's other partners. Having Ghost-type Pokemon in the back such as Basculegion-M and Sinistcha as switch-ins to Sneasler's Close Combat is a good idea to cover for Kingambit's Fighting weakness. It is a good idea to have Garchomp and Kingambit on the field at the same time, as they perfectly cover for each other's weaknesses; Kingambit covers Pokemon such as Alolan Ninetales, Mega Froslass, and Mega Gardevoir, while Garchomp handles Pokemon such as Mega Charizard Y, Sneasler, and opposing Kingambit.","source_format":"champions/vgc-2026-regulation-m-a"}
