 {"species":"farigiraf","moves":["protect","psychic","thunderbolt","trickroom"],"item":"colburberry","regulation":"champions-reg-ma","spread":{"hp":30,"atk":0,"def":24,"spa":0,"spd":12,"spe":0},"source_tier":"champions_native_writeup","verified":false,"verification_context":{},"date_resolved":"2026-07-27T18:28:21Z","variants":[{"hp":12,"atk":0,"def":24,"spa":27,"spd":3,"spe":0}],"rationale":"Farigiraf's solid resilience and unique ability to deny Fake Out give it a strong niche as a reliable Trick Room setter. Offensively, a Psychic typing grants it a great matchup against Poison-types like Sneasler, Glimmora, and Venusaur. Psychic: Even with no Special Attack investment, Psychic will always 2HKO maximum HP variants of Mega Gengar and Mega Venusaur. Thunderbolt vs. Hyper Voice: Thunderbolt pressures Flying- and Water-types like Mega Charizard Y, Mega Aerodactyl, and Basculegion-M, notably having a good chance to 2HKO the latter two with no investment. Hyper Voice sacrifices useful coverage for the ability to constantly pressure the opposing team with spread damage, especially if Farigiraf has the initiative under Trick Room. Protect vs. Helping Hand: If Farigiraf's support is integral to your team, it can use Protect to defensively position itself and guard against double targeting. Helping Hand can be used over Protect if you can afford to sacrifice Farigiraf, allowing it to bolster the team's damage output even when it's about to be KOed. Farigiraf can run both moves in the last two moveslots only if it's supporting a Pokemon that can deal so much spread damage, like Torkoal or Mega Blastoise, that having an auxiliary attack isn't necessary. Other Options Twin Beam: Twin Beam is a weaker alternative to Psychic that's capable of OHKOing Focus Sash variants of Sneasler and, with enough investment, Glimmora. Roar: Roar can be used in the last moveslot to deny setup sweepers like Mega Floette from gaining boosts and users of Trick Room like Sinistcha and opposing Farigiraf from setting it up. Ally Switch: Although it's reliant on predicting your opponent's actions, Ally Switch's ability to essentially redirect an incoming attack away from Farigiraf's ally can make it a worthwhile consideration for the last moveslot. Items Sitrus Berry: Sitrus Berry's burst healing lets Farigiraf repeatedly survive strong attacks like Sneasler's Close Combat and handle double targeting much more easily, making it the preferred held item. Colbur Berry: If Sitrus Berry isn't available, Colbur Berry can be used to guarantee survival against Black Glasses Kingambit's Kowtow Cleave and Mega Tyranitar's Knock Off. Abilities Armor Tail: Armor Tail's most notable application is denying Fake Out from users like Sneasler and Incineroar. Additionally, it protects Farigiraf's team from Kingambit's Sucker Punch and Prankster-boosted moves like Whimsicott's Encore and Sableye's Quash. SP Spreads Speed-reducing Natures: A Relaxed, Quiet, or Sassy nature can be used over a Bold, Modest, or Calm nature, respectively, if you want Farigiraf to outspeed neutral-natured base 60s like Sylveon and Incineroar under Trick Room. 30 HP / 24 Def / 12 SpD with Bold or Relaxed: This is a physically defensive spread that lets Farigiraf survive Black Glasses Kingambit's Kowtow Cleave and Mega Scizor's Bug Bite. With Sitrus Berry, Farigiraf is also likely to avoid getting 2HKOed by Sneasler's Close Combat, Jolly Adaptability Basculegion-M's Wave Crash, and Modest Mega Floette's Dazzling Gleam. 12 HP / 24 Def / 27 SpA / 3 SpD with Modest or Quiet: This offensive spread lets Farigiraf usually OHKO Focus Sash Glimmora with Twin Beam and potentially OHKO maximum HP Mega Gengar with Psychic. The bulk investment lets Farigiraf avoid the OHKO from non-Black Glasses Kingambit's Kowtow Cleave and Mega Floette's Moonblast, as well as the 2HKO from uninvested Incineroar's Throat Chop with either Berry. 32 HP / 11 Def / 23 SpD with Calm or Sassy: With the heavy special bulk investment, Farigiraf cannot be OHKOed by Mega Floette's Light of Ruin and is unlikely to be OHKOed by its +1 Moonblast, while 11 Defense SPs give favorable odds to survive non-Black Glasses Kingambit's Kowtow Cleave. Sitrus Berry lets Farigiraf dodge the 2HKO from Mega Charizard Y's Heat Wave and Archaludon's Electro Shot, as well as the 3HKO from Jolly Garchomp's Dragon Claw almost all of the time. Teambuilding Checks and Weaknesses: Kingambit is the most threatening Pokemon to Farigiraf, as it can easily KO non-Colbur Berry variants with Kowtow Cleave, comfortably take Farigiraf's STAB attacks, and benefit from Trick Room with its low Speed. Additionally, Farigiraf is a sitting duck against other Dark-types like Mega Tyranitar and Incineroar; Mega Tyranitar can threaten an OHKO with Knock Off and proceed to set up as it switches out, while Incineroar can gradually wear it down and lock out Hyper Voice with Throat Chop. Steel-types like Aegislash and Corviknight easily tank Farigiraf's STAB attacks, which lets them freely attack and, in Corviknight's case, set up. Bug-types like Kleavor and Mega Scizor pressure Farigiraf with their STAB moves; additionally, Mega Scizor can set up Swords Dance and gain free recovery by eating its Sitrus Berry with Bug Bite. Although it's fairly bulky, Farigiraf can be easily KOed if it's targeted by a pair of very strong foes; a combination of attacks like Mega Charizard Y's Weather Ball and Sneasler's Close Combat can put it out of commission if it attempts to set up Trick Room. Farigiraf's lack of coverage and Speed can make it passive outside of Trick Room, especially if it uses a bulky SP spread. This can put the burden on its on-field ally to pick up the slack offensively, which the opponent can exploit by double targeting the ally. Good Partners and Synergies: Farigiraf should be ideally paired with slow teammates like Kingambit and Sylveon, as they appreciate the ability to attack first and still tank a couple blows with their bulk investment. However, it's possible to use Farigiraf alongside moderately fast Pokemon like Mega Charizard Y and Mega Floette, especially if the opposing team uses Tailwind support. In this case, a Tailwind setter like Whimsicott or Aerodactyl can be beneficial for an alternate team mode if Trick Room isn't needed, and Farigiraf can still contribute to this mode by blocking Fake Out with Armor Tail to preserve the setter's Focus Sash. This also prevents Pokemon that don't run Protect, like Choice Scarf Garchomp and most Chople Berry Kingambit variants, from getting disrupted and losing momentum. Kingambit appreciates Farigiraf's ability to pressure Sneasler; in return, it can handle Aegislash and, with Low Kick, other Dark-types like opposing Kingambit and Mega Tyranitar. Fairy-types like Sylveon and Mega Floette can repay Farigiraf's good matchup against Poison-types by handling Dark-types for it; Sylveon can use Trick Room to attack unimpeded, while bulky Calm Mind variants of Mega Floette can have an easier time setting up under it. Fire-types like Torkoal and Mega Charizard Y can blast through Steel- and Bug-types with their STAB moves. Torkoal especially stands out given its absolutely subpar Speed, which, in tandem with Armor Tail, makes it almost guaranteed to unleash a full-power Eruption under Trick Room. Incineroar can also handle these foes itself under Trick Room, and it can help protect Farigiraf from getting overwhelmed with Fake Out, Intimidate, and Parting Shot. How to Overcome Farigiraf's Weaknesses: Farigiraf should be positioned in a way such that it won't be KOed if it attempts to set up Trick Room. When paired with it as the leading duo, Incineroar can prevent double targeting with Fake Out, letting Farigiraf set up Trick Room more easily. Once Trick Room is set up, Incineroar can pivot to an offensive teammate to maintain momentum. Under Trick Room, Farigiraf should ideally be paired with the teammate that threatens the opposing side the best or switch out if two offensive Pokemon can put up better pressure. Outside of Trick Room, it can get around its Speed with Helping Hand to still contribute to the team's damage output. If your team has a Tailwind setter alongside Farigiraf, determine the opposing team's means of speed control and potential priority users during Team Preview, then play off your selections from there. For example, if the opposing team has its own Tailwind setter and a Fake Out user, it may be wise to bench your setter and bring Farigiraf instead.","source_format":"champions/vgc-2026-regulation-m-a"}
 {"species":"sneasler","moves":["closecombat","direclaw","fakeout","protect"],"item":"whiteherb","regulation":"champions-reg-ma","spread":{"hp":2,"atk":32,"def":0,"spa":0,"spd":0,"spe":32},"source_tier":"champions_native_writeup","verified":false,"verification_context":{},"date_resolved":"2026-07-27T18:28:21Z","rationale":"Sneasler is the fastest relevant Fake Out user in Regulation M-A, guaranteeing a threat will be halted so that Sneasler's ally can move safely, and it's undoubtedly the fastest Pokemon in the format with Unburden active. Thanks to its STAB combination, Sneasler also threatens many prominent Pokemon like Kingambit, Mega Floette, and Sylveon. Close Combat: In addition to handling Dark- and Normal-types like Incineroar, Mega Tyranitar, and Maushold, Close Combat's drawback can be used with White Herb to grant Sneasler unparalleled Speed. Dire Claw: Though it shouldn't be relied upon, Dire Claw's suite of status conditions can potentially push a critical situation in your favor. Other Options Coaching: Coaching can be slotted over Protect to provide support to physically offensive teammates like Garchomp, as the extra power and bulk granted to such Pokemon can justify the inability to make defensive plays. Rock-type Coverage: Rock Slide and Rock Tomb can be considered to severely damage Mega Charizard Y and Talonflame. Rock Slide deals spread damage and can let you game for flinches, while Rock Tomb is a more reliable alternative that trades damage output for the potential to let Sneasler's teammates hit an otherwise faster foe like Mega Froslass before it moves. Throat Chop: Throat Chop lets Sneasler threaten Ghost-types like Aegislash and Mega Gengar and act as a late-game emergency check to Choice Scarf Basculegion-M with Focus Sash. Gunk Shot: Although it's less accurate than Dire Claw, Gunk Shot's ability to let even Jolly Sneasler one-shot most bulky variants of Mega Floette and Sylveon makes it worth considering. Additionally, Adamant Sneasler's Gunk Shot is very likely to OHKO Mega Delphox. Items White Herb: White Herb is the most common item on Sneasler, as the item grants it on-demand speed control with use of Close Combat. White Herb also gives it a buffer against stat drops incurred by Incineroar's Intimidate and Milotic's Icy Wind. Focus Sash: Focus Sash generally ensures Sneasler will make at least one move before fainting, though it'll be harder to activate Unburden without a would-be fatal blow. Focus Sash is also a contested item that teammates like Aerodactyl may need to function effectively. Abilities Unburden: Unburden's Speed boost is crucial to outspeed faster foes like Choice Scarf Garchomp, Sand Rush Excadrill, and Chlorophyll Venusaur. SP Spreads 2 HP / 32 Atk / 32 Spe with Adamant or Jolly: An Adamant nature lets Sneasler OHKO maximum HP Sylveon with Dire Claw and have a favored chance to OHKO Chople Berry Kingambit with Close Combat while still outspeeding neutral-natured weather attackers like Venusaur and Excadrill with Unburden active. A Jolly nature allows Sneasler to outspeed opposing Adamant Sneasler, Maushold, and Alolan Ninetales, letting it use Fake Out first against the former; note that positive-natured variants of Venusaur and Excadrill are uncommon. 32 HP / 4 Atk / 29 Def / 1 Spe with Jolly: A bulky spread is an option on White Herb sets to allow Sneasler to survive otherwise deadly attacks and still pack enough power to 2HKO neutral foes like Garchomp with Close Combat. This spread allows it to survive Aerodactyl's and Sharp Beak Talonflame's Dual Wingbeat and Garchomp's Stomping Tantrum while outspeeding Adamant Garchomp and Modest Mega Floette, as well as Jolly Sand Rush Excadrill with Unburden active. Teambuilding Checks and Weaknesses: Sneasler is walled by Ghost-types like Basculegion-M and Aegislash; they resist Dire Claw and ignore Fake Out and Close Combat, letting them safely come in on predicted attacks. Mega Gengar is a very threatening Ghost-type, as Gengar can force Sneasler out and Mega Evolve to trap its teammates. Sinistcha, in particular, can set up Trick Room and render Sneasler very vulnerable to attacks; Farigiraf accomplishes the same while preventing Fake Out from hitting its team and directly threatening it with Psychic or Twin Beam. Without Unburden active, faster attackers like Choice Scarf Garchomp, Sand Rush Excadrill, Mega Delphox, and Aerodactyl can easily OHKO it, with the latter even bypassing Focus Sash with Dual Wingbeat and matching Unburden with Tailwind. Good Partners and Synergies: Kingambit is one of the best partners for Sneasler, as it threatens Ghost-types and prominent Trick Room setters with its STAB Dark-type moves. Basculegion-M appreciates Sneasler's good matchup against opposing Kingambit, which can threaten its late-game sweeps with Sucker Punch, while Dragon-types like Garchomp and Archaludon can safely let their STAB moves loose with opposing Fairy-types removed by Sneasler. How to Overcome Sneasler's Weaknesses: Choosing Kingambit during Team Preview will give Sneasler security when facing Ghost-types alongside it or ensure you have a reliable switch-in to them. Kingambit also benefits from Trick Room, making it a potential counterlead against Sinistcha and Farigiraf. Against faster threats, aim to have Unburden activated by the time they come out; if that's not plausible, priority moves like Kingambit's Sucker Punch can help lessen their Speed advantage. Weather setters like Mega Charizard Y can also nullify the Speed advantage of opposing weather attackers like Excadrill, though keep in mind that opponents will often attempt to fight for weather control with their own setters like Mega Tyranitar.","source_format":"champions/vgc-2026-regulation-m-a"}
