on, and Trick Room speed control. Sableye gives Archaludon more bulk via dual screens while using moves such as Rain Dance, Encore, Disable, and Will-O-Wisp to disrupt foes. Rain Dance is used in weather wars, Encore can lock foes like Sneasler into Fake Out and Pokemon that may threaten Archaludon into Protect, Disable can prevent attacks such as Sneasler's Close Combat from threatening Archaludon and can force Choice Scarf users to use Struggle, and Will-O-Wisp can harm physical attackers. How to Overcome Archaludon's Weaknesses: Archaludon's weakness to Sneasler's and Kommo-o's Fighting-type STAB moves can be patched up by threatening these Fighting-types with Pelipper's Hurricane, redirecting attacks with Sinistcha's Rage Powder, or switching Basculegion-M or Sinistcha into Sneasler's Close Combat and Kommo-o's Aura Sphere. Basculegion-M can heavily damage Garchomp with Adaptability-boosted Wave Crash or Last Respects after two or three allies have fainted. Archaludon's mediocre Special Defense can be patched up with Sableye's Light Screen and Special Defense boosts from Espathra's Calm Mind. Archaludon needs rain to set up with Electro Shot; therefore, having a manual Rain Dance user like Sableye alongside setters like Pelipper is great for keeping weather control when facing Mega Charizard Y.","source_format":"champions/vgc-2026-regulation-m-a","nature":"Modest"}
